-- One hop of the forward pass: from an entity, through a relation band, to the
-- entity nearest that band's attention centroid.
--
-- TIER SCOPE (2026-08-05, GH #868). The step now stays at the subject's own tier.
-- A forward step is a move among peers — word to word, sentence to sentence.
-- Previously the KNN ran over every tier in laplace.v_word_points with no tier predicate,
-- so a step from a word could land on a codepoint, a sentence or a document.
--
-- That was not theoretical. This function could never return a row at all: its
-- `WHERE c.total_weight > 0` was evaluated against a centroid that was NULL on
-- every call (GH #866), so the forward path was dead from the day it was written.
-- When #866 made the centroid real and c2bc4c55 projected it back onto S³ as a
-- proper Fréchet/Karcher mean, the comparison point moved from the interior onto
-- the unit shell — the one neighbourhood tier 0 occupies exclusively, since
-- super_fibonacci seeds codepoints at radius exactly 1 while every composed coord
-- is a centroid and therefore interior. The first thing this ever returned for
-- 'dog' was a two-character entity.
--
-- NO THRESHOLD. laplace_attention_centroid now also returns `concentration` — 1.0
-- when every attended point coincides, approaching 0 when they cancel and the
-- centroid has no direction at all. It is deliberately NOT used here as a cutoff:
-- spec 37 L6 forbids operator floors, and "abstain below 0.3" would be exactly
-- that. The one case handled is the genuinely degenerate one — concentration 0
-- yields NULL coordinates, because a cancelled sum has no direction to point in,
-- and abstaining there is a fact about the data rather than a tuned threshold.
--
-- No SET search_path (GH #860). This body is scalar and carries a FROM clause, so
-- the scalar inliner rejects it either way; the clause is unjustified regardless
-- and its presence would be one more site for the sweep.
DROP FUNCTION IF EXISTS laplace.laplace_forward_step(bytea, bytea);
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION generation.laplace_forward_step(
    p_entity   bytea,
    p_band_mask bytea)
RETURNS bytea
LANGUAGE sql STABLE PARALLEL RESTRICTED AS $$
    SELECT n.entity_id
    FROM generation.laplace_attention_centroid(p_entity, p_band_mask) c
    JOIN LATERAL generation.laplace_nearest_entity(
             c.cx, c.cy, c.cz, c.cm, 1, p_band_mask,
             ARRAY[generation.entity_tier_of(p_entity)::smallint]) n ON TRUE
    WHERE c.total_weight > 0
      AND c.cx IS NOT NULL          -- concentration 0 => no direction => abstain
      AND n.entity_id IS NOT NULL
      AND n.entity_id <> p_entity
    -- No LIMIT: the k argument to laplace_nearest_entity IS the cap (k = 1), and
    -- the KNN ranks before it cuts. A trailing LIMIT 1 read as a safeguard over an
    -- unordered pick, which is the opposite of what this call does -- and it could
    -- not have guarded the one real edge case anyway, since the self-match filter
    -- runs after the k = 1 pick and correctly yields no row.
$$;
